meta {
  name: Share Order Report All
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/share-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "patient@example.com",
    "sms": "919999999999",
    "whatsapp": "919999999999"
  }
}

docs {
  "Share All" from the Order Console: queue the order's lab report to the patient
  over EVERY channel the tenant has ACTIVATED a `console_lab_report_as_attachment`
  template for — Email, SMS, WhatsApp AND the in-app message (IAM) — in one call.

  - Body is optional. `email` / `sms` / `whatsapp` override the auto-filled
    recipient for that channel (blank = the patient's stored contact). IAM has no
    address — it targets the patient's in-app inbox.

  Each channel is attempted independently and never aborts the others:
  - QUEUED  — handed to the queue (Email/SMS/WhatsApp) or created in-app (IAM).
  - SKIPPED — no activated template for the channel, or no recipient on file.
  - FAILED  — an error (e.g. template missing DLT/WhatsApp provider settings).

  Email/WhatsApp attach the rendered `lab_all_report` PDF (rendered once, reused).
  Returns `{ orderId, results: [{ channel, status, reason?, logId? }] }`.
  `logId` is a communication_logs id (deliverable channels) or a notification id (IAM).

  Prereqs: activated messaging templates (per channel) for the feature, and an
  active `lab_all_report` PDF template so Email/WhatsApp can render.
}
